    description: "INV-zuhub item 1, edge-type family 'module_exports'. Audit the 1 linker that emits module_exports edges (linkers/js_module.py:807 Edge.create) to determine whether a simple-name fallback resolution path exists.\n\nPreliminary read: the module_exports edges at js_module.py:799-816 use symbols_by_file.get(resolved_str, ...) — symbols are filtered by file path with no short-name matching. The resolution is precision-only; no fallback decision happens. If this read is confirmed by deeper audit, this WI closes vacuously with documentation noting the family has no fallback shape to gate; the three property-test shapes (prefers_imported / same_file_preferred / deterministic_fallback) would have no behavior to exercise.\n\nIf the audit surfaces a hidden fallback path (e.g. a name-collision short-circuit not visible in the immediate call site), apply the canonical inheritance.py pattern (thread is_fallback bool through resolver; set conf<=0.5 + meta[disambiguation_fallback]=True at edge-creation) and add the three property tests.\n\nParent: INV-zuhub. Pre-condition: commit dd2a93550e (foundation PR) merged."  # d0fd
