- op: discuss  # 9230
  at: '2026-05-12T02:05:12Z'  # 9230
  by: agent  # 9230
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9230
  clock: 4  # 9230
  nonce: '9230'  # 9230
  message: "Closing as done with audit evidence. The module_exports edge family has no simple-name fallback resolution path — INV-zuhub item 1 is vacuous for this family.\n\nAudit findings (linkers/js_module.py):\n\n1. **module_exports emission (lines 799-816)**: dst is resolved by file-path keyed lookup (`symbols_by_file.get(resolved_str, ...)`). The resolution chain is:\n   - Earlier in the function, `resolved_str` is computed from `_resolve_relative_import` / `_resolve_alias_import` — both return concrete file paths.\n   - Symbol set comes from `symbols_by_file` indexed by full path.\n   - Edge.create at line 807 emits one edge per file_sym in the resolved file.\n   No short-name collision possibility — the keying dimension is file path, not symbol name.\n\n2. **Adjacent imports / imports_module emission (lines 788-797)**: dst is `mod_sym.id` from `module_file_cache[rel_path]` — keyed by file path. `import_confidence` is 0.90 (relative imports) or 0.85 (alias resolution); both above the 0.5 ceiling. The medium-high confidence reflects path-resolution reliability, not fallback decision.\n\n3. **npm_package imports (lines 818-857)**: dst is `pkg_sym.id` from `npm_package_cache[pkg_name]` — keyed by package name extracted from the import statement, not short-symbol-name matching across the symbol table.\n\nThe 0.75 confidence on module_exports (line 815) reflects the structural over-approximation 'every symbol in the imported file is exported from it' — a heuristic uncertainty, not a short-name disambiguation. INV-zuhub addresses a different failure class (cross-package short-name collisions), so the disambiguation_fallback meta flag would be semantically wrong to set here.\n\nConclusion: js_module.py is precision-only by construction; the three INV-zuhub property test shapes (test_module_exports_prefers_imported_*, test_module_exports_same_file_preferred_over_other_file, test_module_exports_deterministic_fallback_when_ambiguous) have no behavior to exercise — every module_exports edge is deterministically file-path-resolved. The flagless-fallback failure mode INV-zuhub addresses cannot occur in this linker.\n\nNo code change needed. Foundation gate (PR dd2a93550e) continues to enforce the contract for any future linker that DOES set the flag, including hypothetical future module_exports producers."  # 9230
